# Environment isolation — never commit the local interpreter / venv
.venv/
.venv-engine/
# LTX 2.5 engine interpreter. A SECOND engine venv, not a replacement: the two
# stacks need incompatible transformers majors (4.x vs 5.x), so they cannot
# share one interpreter. Built by scripts/install_ltx.ps1 (Ensure-EngineVenv).
.venv-engine-ltx25/
# Utility-AI interpreter (object tracking / UETrack). A THIRD venv, built only
# when someone runs install-UETrack.bat: CPU-only torch, so it must not share
# an interpreter with either cu128 engine stack.
.venv-utils/
.python/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# Runtime data
outputs/*
!outputs/.gitkeep
uploads/*
!uploads/.gitkeep
logs/*
!logs/.gitkeep
# models/ はベースモデル優先レイアウト(2階層以上)。models/* だと2階層目以降の
# ファイルが無視から漏れず追跡されてしまう罠があるため、階層全体を無視した上で
# ディレクトリ自体(!models/**/)を再包含している。これが無いとgitが配下を走査せず、
# put_*_here.txt(案内ファイル)まで無視されてしまう。
models/**
!models/**/
!models/**/put_*_here.txt
!models/.gitkeep

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Heavy LTX data — MUST NEVER reach the GitHub repo.
# These are installed locally by scripts/install_ltx.ps1.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The engine is first-party (project-root ./engine, git-tracked), so no vendor
# negation is needed. Everything under vendor/ is ignored. The official LTX-2
# clone (vendor/LTX-2) is a re-cloneable upstream reference kept out of the repo.
# Engine provenance: engine/VENDOR_NOTICE.md.
vendor/*

# Model weights / large binary artifacts (safety net regardless of location)
*.safetensors
*.ckpt
*.pt
*.pth
*.bin
*.gguf
*.onnx
*.npz
*.tar
*.zip
# Wheels built by scripts/build_xformers.ps1
*.whl

# HuggingFace / uv caches inside the project (install_ltx.ps1 points HF_HOME at
# hf_home/ and UV_CACHE_DIR at .uv_cache/), plus other local cache directories
.cache/
hf_home/
.uv_cache/

# uv lockfile (resolved per-machine here)
uv.lock

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local per-machine artifacts — never committed
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# User-edited configuration. Tracking it would make every `git pull` stop on a
# merge conflict against the settings the user tuned for their own machine.
# The template that ships with the repo is config.yaml.example; setup.bat and
# run.bat copy it into place when config.yaml is missing.
config.yaml
# The backup install_ltx.ps1 writes before it rewrites model paths in config.yaml.
config.yaml.bak

# Server RUNTIME STATE (services/runtime_state.py): the last active base model
# and model selection, rewritten on every successful pipeline load. Per-machine
# and disposable -- deleting it just brings back the shipped defaults -- so it
# must never be committed. The .bad sibling is the copy set aside when the file
# turns out to be unreadable.
/state.json
/state.json.bad

# Prerequisite tools fetched by setup.bat (uv + ffmpeg/ffprobe), ~378 MB on disk.
# Leading slash: root-only, so this must never shadow mcp_server/tools/ (the
# MCP server's own source package) or any other nested tools/ directory.
/tools/

# Generated by setup.ps1 with ABSOLUTE, machine-specific paths (this machine's
# .venv\Scripts\python.exe). Committing it would break every other machine's
# MCP registration and leak local filesystem layout. See scripts/setup.ps1 /
# README "AIエージェント連携（MCPサーバー）".
.mcp.json

# ローカルのエージェント設定・個人環境パスを含むため追跡除外
.claude/
